00:56:51.630 --> 00:56:58.660
It's like, it seems to me that the 20th century
will be remembered for the hydrogen bomb,

00:56:58.660 --> 00:57:01.119
the transistor, and the birth control pill.

00:57:01.119 --> 00:57:05.480
And those are unbelievably radical technological
innovations, and maybe the most...

00:57:05.480 --> 00:57:06.480
Christina: Internet.

00:57:06.480 --> 00:57:07.480
Internet came in.

00:57:07.480 --> 00:57:08.480
Jordan: Yeah, but it's dependent...

00:57:08.480 --> 00:57:09.480
Christina: My Fair Lady?

00:57:09.480 --> 00:57:10.480
My Fair Lady?

00:57:10.480 --> 00:57:11.480
Just saying...

00:57:11.480 --> 00:57:13.799
Jordan: ...it's dependent on the transistor,
you know, because it spawned all of that.

00:57:13.799 --> 00:57:17.010
So that's the big technological innovation
that spawned all that.

00:57:17.010 --> 00:57:23.650
And of the three, I would say the birth control
pill is probably the bigger hydrogen bomb.

00:57:23.650 --> 00:57:30.450
Because it changed the fundamental biological
nature of women and men.

00:57:30.450 --> 00:57:38.339
And because it gave women, for the first time
